-- CONTROL fixture for the future D-CYCLE / D-RECURSIVE checks (spec §6.4.2,
-- §6.4.4-5). One of eleven files covering the nine cycle shapes; read
-- jl4/examples/dmn/README.md's cycle table for the set.
--
-- p1: a FORWARD REFERENCE and nothing more. `the headline figure` is defined
-- before `the base figure`, which it reads. The DRG edge runs base -> headline
-- and the graph is GENUINELY ACYCLIC.
--
-- This is the file that proves the SCC does not cry wolf. Every other fixture
-- in the set asserts that something IS reported; without this one, a detector
-- that reported every node would pass all ten of them.
--
-- Expected after Phase 4: NO D-CYCLE and NO D-RECURSIVE. (On today's tree the
-- fidelity report carries D-SCOPE and two D-LITERALEXPR notes, which are
-- unrelated to the cycle question and are not what this fixture asserts.)
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `forward reference only`

ASSUME `the reported amount` IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the headline figure` MEANS
    `the base figure` TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base figure` MEANS
    `the reported amount` PLUS 1
